<!-- Ata Hero online update feed. UpdateService reads this on every launch.
     Each release: bump <version> and point <url> at the new setup exe.
     <version> must be > the installed AssemblyVersion to trigger an update.

     !! THE TAG IS CASE-SENSITIVE AND IS NOT THE RELEASE TITLE !!
     GitHub download URLs use the TAG, matched exactly. Get it wrong and the
     app says "This version's installer isn't on the download page yet" — the
     client HEAD-checks the URL before offering the download, so a bad tag
     looks like a missing installer.

     TAGS SO FAR, because they are not consistent and guessing has failed twice:
         1.0.16  V1.0.16   capital V
         1.0.17  v1.0.17   lowercase
         1.0.18  v.1.0.18  lowercase, WITH A DOT AFTER THE v

     5 Oct 2026: this note once claimed 1.0.17's tag was "V1.0.17". It was not,
     the feed was written to match the comment instead of the release page, and
     nobody could download 1.0.17.
     18 Oct 2026: 1.0.18 was tagged "v.1.0.18" while the release TITLE reads
     "v1.0.18". The title is decoration; the tag is the URL. Open the release
     page and read the tag chip — do not copy it from here.

     <game> — the download-page game. OPTIONAL. Leave it out and the version
     number picks one by rotation. Slugs are in AppUpdate\Games\UpdateGame.cs;
     an unknown name is ignored and rotates instead.

     18 Oct 2026: the game is now CHOSEN BY HAND, walking the list top to
     bottom, rather than left to the version rotation. Steady hand was skipped
     for having had a long run. Order from here: hangman (1.0.18), memory,
     reaction, scramble, simon, higher-lower, odd-one-out, quick-maths, xo,
     riddles, fill-in, movies, then steady-hand comes back round.

     !! ONCE PINNED BY HAND, KEEP PINNING. The rotation is no longer in step.
     Forget the tag on 1.0.19 and it jumps to xo (10019 % 13 = 9), not memory.

     The game is read from the feed at download time by the client the person
     is CURRENTLY running, so this line can be changed any time without a
     rebuild — and it changes what 1.0.18's download page plays. -->
<item>
  <version>1.0.18.0</version>
  <url>https://github.com/nashryle/AtaHero/releases/download/v.1.0.18/AtaHeroSetup-1.0.18.exe</url>
  <changelog>https://github.com/nashryle/AtaHero/releases/tag/v.1.0.18</changelog>
  <mandatory mode="0">false</mandatory>
  <game>hangman</game>
</item>
